sec.p:
X‐ray crystallography: Suitable crystals for [Pt(L1
)(acac)], [Pt(L2
)(acac)] and [Pt(L3
)(acac)] were obtained and mounted on a MITIGEN holder in oil on either a Rigaku 007HF diffractometer equipped with HF Varimax confocal mirrors and an AFC11 goniometer and HyPix 6000HE detector ([Pt(L1
)(acac)]), or a Rigaku FRE+ diffractometer equipped with Arc)Sec VHF Varimax confocal mirrors and either an AFC12 goniometer and HyPix 6000 detector ([Pt(L2
)(acac)]_200 K) or with a UG2 goniometer and HyPix 6000HE detector ([Pt(L2
)(acac)]_100 K and [Pt(L3
)(acac)]).
[57]
 Using Olex2
[58]
 the structure was solved with the ShelXT
[59]
 structure solution program, using the Intrinsic Phasing solution method. The model was refined with version 2014/7 of ShelXL
[60]
 using Least Squares minimisation. All non‐H atoms were refined anisotropically and difference Fourier syntheses were employed in positioning idealized hydrogen atoms and were allowed to ride on their parent C‐atoms.

